---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";
import SocialProof from "../components/SocialProof.astro";

const title = "FUNMILY Treadmill (2026): Walking Pads, Desk Treadmill and Manuals";
const description =
  "Is a FUNMILY treadmill or walking pad worth buying? FUNMILY’s range checked on 5 November 2026, where its figures conflict, how to find the manual, and checked alternatives.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: "funmily-12-incline-walking-pad",
    name: "FUNMILY Walking Pad Treadmill with Incline and Handle Bar",
    category: "Walking Pad With Handle and Manual Incline",
    badge: "Most Common FUNMILY",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=FUNMILY+Walking+Pad+Treadmill+with+Incline+and+Handle+Bar&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: null,
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "Price not confirmed on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: null,
    specs: "Handle bar · manual incline (12% per FUNMILY) · 0.6–4.0 mph per the Amazon listing · motor and capacity conflict",
    pros: [
      "A handle bar and a manual incline on a pad that slides under a desk",
      "Remote control and LED display",
      "FUNMILY states a 12-month parts and labor warranty",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Motor given as 2.5 HP by FUNMILY and 3.5 HP on Amazon",
      "Capacity given as 300, 350 and 400 lb by different sources",
      "Amazon’s listing gives a 35 x 15-inch belt, short and narrow",
    ],
    bottomLine: "Only worth it at a clearly lower price than the checked pads, and only for walking, given how much its figures move.",
    description: "This is the FUNMILY pad most often seen on deal sites: a walking pad with a short handle bar, a remote and a manual incline. FUNMILY’s website lists a “Walking Pad Treadmill with Incline (12%)” with a 2.5 HP brushless motor, a dual-position incline to 12%, a 16-inch belt width, a 300 lb capacity and a 5.9-inch profile. A Slickdeals post from 25 May 2026 quotes the Amazon listing, at $143.99 after a coupon, as a 3.5 HP brushless pad with a 350 lb capacity, a 35 by 15-inch belt, 0.6 to 4.0 mph and a one-year warranty, and a listing summary for a pink FUNMILY 12% pad gives 3.5 HP and 400 lb. Slickdeals commenters also said the review photos appeared to show a different model. With three capacities and two motor ratings, the card gives neither: assume 300 lb at most.",
  },
  {
    id: "funmily-treadmill-desk",
    name: "FUNMILY Treadmill with Desk Workstation",
    category: "Walking Treadmill With Built-In Desk",
    badge: "Best for Desk Work",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=FUNMILY+Treadmill+with+Desk+Workstation&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: null,
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "Price not confirmed on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: null,
    specs: "Built-in height-adjustable desk · 0.6–7.5 mph · 3-level incline · 2.5 HP advertised",
    pros: [
      "A desk surface built in, so you do not need a standing desk",
      "FUNMILY and ShopSavvy agree on 7.5 mph and three incline levels",
      "Folds for storage, according to FUNMILY",
    ],
    cons: [
      "FUNMILY’s own page gives the capacity as 300 lb and 265 lb",
      "Buyers report it is heavy and hard to move, with timer and support complaints",
      "ShopSavvy’s aggregated score was 5.9 out of 10",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For someone without a standing desk who wants an all-in-one walking workstation and accepts a budget build.",
    description: "FUNMILY’s treadmill desk combines a walking treadmill with a desk surface on the handlebar. FUNMILY’s website lists it with a 2.5 HP motor, 0.6 to 7.5 mph, a three-level incline that it describes as up to 4%, a 7-layer belt and a desk that adjusts from 33.5 to 49.9 inches, and gives the capacity as 300 lb in one section and 265 lb in another, for what appear to be two versions. ShopSavvy’s aggregated review page, last updated in October 2024 when it saw the treadmill at $272.60, gives the same 7.5 mph, three incline levels and 300 lb, and a score of 5.9 out of 10: buyers praise easy assembly and quiet running but report weight, timer faults, units that did not work and poor customer service. Our treadmill desks roundup covers sturdier options.",
  },
  {
    id: "funmily-5-incline-walking-pad",
    name: "FUNMILY Smallest Walking Pad with 5% Incline",
    category: "Compact Walking Pad With Fixed Incline",
    badge: "Smallest FUNMILY",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=FUNMILY+Walking+Pad+5%25+Incline&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: null,
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "Price not confirmed on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: null,
    specs: "Fixed 5% incline · 0.6–4.0 mph (maker) · 2.5 HP advertised · no handle",
    pros: [
      "A built-in gentle incline, so every walk is slightly uphill",
      "Sold as needing no assembly",
      "Small enough for a narrow space under a desk",
    ],
    cons: [
      "FUNMILY gives 41 x 25 x 8 inches and a reseller 37 x 22.4 x 6.7, so no size is printed",
      "The incline is fixed; it cannot be lowered to flat",
      "No independent confirmation of its 300 lb capacity",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a light walker who wants a slight, permanent incline at a desk; check the dimensions on the listing before you buy.",
    description: "FUNMILY’s website lists a “Smallest Under Desk Treadmill with 5% Incline” with a hidden 2.5 HP motor, 0.6 to 4 mph, a fixed 5% incline, a 300 lb capacity, a 50 lb unit weight and a 41 by 25 by 8-inch size, plus a 2025 version with the same headline figures. A reseller listing for what it calls the FUNMILY F0011 “Smallest Walking Pad With Incline” gives $299.99 and 37 by 22.4 by 6.7 inches, a noticeably smaller machine, so we cannot tell whether they are the same pad. We found no independent source for the 300 lb capacity. The fixed incline is the thing to understand before buying: the deck is always slightly raised at the front, which suits steady desk walking but cannot be set flat.",
  },
  {
    id: "urevo-strol-2e",
    name: "UREVO Strol 2E",
    category: "Checked 2-in-1 Alternative",
    badge: "Cheapest Checked Pad",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HG9D52DC?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ZS3Q+sfdL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$169.99 at UREVO (5 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":169.99,"high":169.99},
    specs: "0.6–6.2 mph with handle up · 265 lb capacity · about 15 x 40 in. belt · no incline",
    pros: [
      "UREVO and two hands-on reviews agree on the 265 lb rating and 6.2 mph",
      "A fold-down handle, like the FUNMILY handle-bar pad",
      "A one-year plus 180-day warranty from a brand with a US store",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No incline",
      "Sources give the belt as 40.1 or 40.2 inches long",
      "Walking speed is capped at 4 mph with the handle folded",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheap handle-bar pad to compare any FUNMILY price against, with figures someone has checked.",
    description: "The Strol 2E is UREVO’s budget 2-in-1 walking pad with a handle that folds flat. UREVO’s US store listed it in stock at $169.99, against $289.99, on 5 November 2026, with 0.6 to 4.0 mph with the handle down and 0.6 to 6.2 mph with it raised, a 265 lb maximum load, a 2.25 HP maximum motor rating and a one-year plus 180-day warranty. Live Science and T3, both of which reviewed it hands-on, give the same 265 lb and 6.2 mph. The belt is 40.2 inches long on UREVO’s page and 40.1 in other listings, which is why the card rounds. It has no incline, which is the main thing a FUNMILY pad offers that this does not.",
  },
  {
    id: "merach-novawalk-w50-trekpad",
    name: "MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad",
    category: "Checked Incline Pad Alternative",
    badge: "Best for Heavier Walkers",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJTT2S6R?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41N86eQUrbL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$299.99 at MERACH (5 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":299.99,"high":299.99},
    specs: "41.3 x 16.5 in. belt · 0.6–4.0 mph · 400 lb capacity · 1.25 HP continuous motor · powered incline",
    pros: [
      "A 400 lb rating that holds up across the maker, Amazon and independent coverage",
      "A powered incline and a published continuous motor rating",
      "A two-year warranty, double FUNMILY’s",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No handle bar",
      "Does not fold, and at 69 lb is heavy to move",
      "MERACH gives 12% incline and at least one roundup 10%, so no maximum is printed",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The incline pad to buy if a FUNMILY listing’s high weight limit is what tempted you.",
    description: "If a FUNMILY listing’s 350 or 400 lb claim is what drew you to it, this is the budget incline pad whose high weight limit holds up. MERACH’s product page on 5 November 2026 listed the W50 TrekPad at $299.99, against $479.99, with a 41.3 by 16.5-inch belt, 0.6 to 4.0 mph, a 400 lb maximum user weight, a 1.25 HP continuous and 3.5 HP peak motor, powered incline, a 69.2 lb unit weight, a two-year warranty and 30-day returns. The capacity and belt figures matched the Amazon listing and independent coverage when we checked them in October. MERACH gives 12% incline while a published roundup describes 10%, so the card leaves the maximum out.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "FUNMILY Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/funmily-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is FUNMILY a good treadmill brand?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is a budget brand with a website, a US address and a stated 12-month warranty, which is more than many marketplace names offer. But its website and Amazon listings give the same pads different motors and weight limits, and we found no hands-on review we could rely on, so judge each listing on its own.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Where can I find a FUNMILY treadmill manual?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "FUNMILY does not host manuals on its website. Look first in the “Product guides and documents” section of the Amazon listing you bought from, then ask the seller through Your Orders using the model number on the frame. Third-party sites index FUNMILY manuals by Amazon ASIN; check the model matches.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the weight limit of a FUNMILY walking pad?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on the model and the source. For the 12% incline handle-bar pad we found 300 lb on FUNMILY’s website, 350 lb on Amazon in May 2026 and 400 lb in a listing summary, and one indexed FUNMILY manual gives 100 kg, about 220 lb. Use the lowest figure for your exact model.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What warranty does FUNMILY give?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "FUNMILY’s FAQ says all its fitness equipment comes with a 12-month warranty for parts and labor, and that warranty details are on each Amazon product page. Support runs through Amazon’s Returns & Orders page or the phone number in the product manual.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Has there been a FUNMILY treadmill recall?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "We searched the CPSC recall database for FUNMILY by title and manufacturer on 5 November 2026 and found no recall. Check your model number on the CPSC site, since marketplace products are sometimes recorded under the importer’s name.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is a good alternative to a FUNMILY walking pad?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "On 5 November 2026 the UREVO Strol 2E handle-bar pad was $169.99 at UREVO, with figures confirmed by two hands-on reviews. For an incline and a 400 lb rating that holds up, the MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad was $299.99 at MERACH.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.name.split(" ")[0] },
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 5,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/funmily-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "funmily treadmill",
      "funmily walking pad treadmill",
      "funmily treadmill manual",
      "funmily treadmill with desk",
      "funmily treadmill review",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See the Models", link: "#models" }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <svg class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full opacity-10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <pattern id="dot-pattern-funmilytreadmills" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="2" cy="2" r="1.5" fill="white"></circle>
        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-funmilytreadmills)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Brand Guide
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated November 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          FUNMILY Treadmills: <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">What We Could Confirm</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          FUNMILY sells walking pads, a treadmill with a built-in desk and folding treadmills, almost entirely through Amazon. Its own website lists the range but no prices, and the same FUNMILY pad can carry a 2.5 or 3.5 HP motor and a 300, 350 or 400 lb limit depending on where you read it. Here is what we could confirm on 5 November 2026, where to find a FUNMILY manual, and what to check before you buy.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            The Short Answer
          </a>
          <a href="#manuals" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            FUNMILY Manuals
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">November 5, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="820" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we read FUNMILY’s official website (thefunmily.com), which lists its range
          with specifications and links each product to Amazon but shows no prices, plus its FAQ and
          warranty statement. We cross-checked individual models against a May 2026 Slickdeals post that
          quotes the Amazon listing, ShopSavvy’s aggregated review page for the FUNMILY treadmill desk,
          and listing summaries and manuals indexed by search engines. Amazon, Walmart and the manuals
          site we tried (manuals.plus) returned errors, bot checks or security checks, so we could not
          read a current FUNMILY listing, price or manual directly; no card carries a price. We found no
          hands-on review we could rely on. Figures that conflict are stated as conflicts and kept off
          the cards. We searched the CPSC recall database for FUNMILY by title and manufacturer and
          found no recall. The UREVO and MERACH alternatives were checked against their makers’ US
          stores the same day. We have not tested any of these machines. Prices change often. We earn
          a commission if you buy through the Amazon links on this page; it does not change what we
          say.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8">
      <div class="not-prose bg-orange-50 border border-orange-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-3">Our Top Picks</h2>
        <ul class="list-none m-0 p-0">
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Most Common FUNMILY:</span>
            <a href="#funmily-12-incline-walking-pad" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">FUNMILY Walking Pad Treadmill with Incline and Handle Bar</a>
            <a href="#funmily-12-incline-walking-pad" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Best for Desk Work:</span>
            <a href="#funmily-treadmill-desk" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">FUNMILY Treadmill with Desk Workstation</a>
            <a href="#funmily-treadmill-desk" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Smallest FUNMILY:</span>
            <a href="#funmily-5-incline-walking-pad" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">FUNMILY Smallest Walking Pad with 5% Incline</a>
            <a href="#funmily-5-incline-walking-pad" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Cheapest Checked Pad:</span>
            <a href="#urevo-strol-2e" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">UREVO Strol 2E</a>
            <a href="#urevo-strol-2e" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 py-2 border-b border-orange-100 last:border-0">
            <span class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#FF5A1F]">Best for Heavier Walkers:</span>
            <a href="#merach-novawalk-w50-trekpad" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad</a>
            <a href="#merach-novawalk-w50-trekpad" class="ml-auto text-xs font-bold text-[#0F62FE] no-underline hover:underline">Jump to review &darr;</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. Is a FUNMILY Treadmill Any Good? The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#who-is-funmily" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. Who Makes FUNMILY Treadmills, and Where They Are Sold</a>
          <a href="#models" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. FUNMILY Treadmills and Walking Pads: What We Could Confirm</a>
          <a href="#conflicts" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. Where FUNMILY’s Figures Disagree</a>
          <a href="#manuals" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. How to Find a FUNMILY Treadmill Manual</a>
          <a href="#what-to-check" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">6. What to Check on a FUNMILY Listing Before You Buy</a>
          <a href="#who-should-buy" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">7. Who Should Buy a FUNMILY Treadmill</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">8. Frequently Asked Questions</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A FUNMILY treadmill is most likely something you found on Amazon: a walking pad with an
          incline and a handle bar, a treadmill with a desk on top, or a small folding treadmill, at a
          price well under the brands you have heard of. FUNMILY is a little more substantial than many
          marketplace names: it has a website, a US address and a stated 12-month warranty. But the site
          sends every buyer to Amazon, its own pages disagree with each other, and the Amazon listings
          disagree with the site. This guide sets out what we could confirm, how to find the manual for
          the model you own or are considering, and which checked alternatives cost about the same.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. Is a FUNMILY Treadmill Any Good? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A FUNMILY walking pad can be a usable budget machine for walking, but we could not
            confirm its key figures: FUNMILY’s website and its Amazon listings give the same pad
            different motors and weight limits, and we found no hands-on review we could rely
            on.</strong> If you buy one, buy it from a listing Amazon fulfils, at a clearly lower price
            than the checked alternatives, and assume the lowest weight limit you see.
          </p>
          <p>
            FUNMILY is better documented than the many walking-pad names that exist only as an Amazon
            storefront. It has its own website listing about a dozen products, a business address in
            Bakersfield, California, a FAQ and a stated warranty of 12 months on parts and labor. But the
            website shows no prices and sends every “Check Price” button to Amazon, and support runs
            through Amazon’s Returns &amp; Orders page or the phone number printed in the manual. In
            practice you are buying a marketplace product, and the listing is what you are relying on.
          </p>
          <p>
            The cards below cover the three FUNMILY machines people search for most, with only the
            figures that held up, plus two checked alternatives at similar prices. If you own a FUNMILY
            already and are looking for the manual, skip to the
            <a href="#manuals" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">manuals section</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-funmily" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. Who Makes FUNMILY Treadmills, and Where They Are Sold</h2>
<p>
            FUNMILY describes itself as a home-fitness brand and lists a business address of Seven Oaks,
            Suite 204, Bakersfield, California, on its website, though the ZIP code shown was incomplete
            when we looked. It does not say who manufactures its machines. Like most budget walking-pad
            brands, it almost certainly sources them from factories that supply other labels too, which is
            why near-identical pads appear under several names on Amazon.
          </p>
          <p>
            On 5 November 2026 FUNMILY’s website listed a treadmill with a desk workstation in two
            versions, two compact walking pads with a fixed 5% incline, walking pads with 8% and 12%
            incline, three folding treadmills with 3.25 or 3.5 HP motors and 300 or 400 lb ratings, an
            under-desk elliptical and an archived elliptical. Every product links to Amazon. FUNMILY pads
            also appear on Walmart’s marketplace, where Walmart showed us only a bot check, and on
            international reseller sites that copy Amazon listings.
          </p>
          <p>
            That route to market has consequences. The seller named in Amazon’s buy box handles your
            return, the Amazon listing’s warranty terms are the ones that apply, and the listing can
            change without FUNMILY’s website changing with it, which is one reason the two disagree. Our
            guide to <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">buying a treadmill on Amazon</a>
            explains what to look for in the buy box, and our
            <a href="/walmart-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Walmart treadmills</a> guide
            covers marketplace sellers there.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="models" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. FUNMILY Treadmills and Walking Pads: What We Could Confirm</h2>
<p>
